# chat_smoke.uaw — chat round-trip smoke with model-down reporting.
#
# Precondition (runner): target build installed, launched, sitting on the
# chat screen.
#
# Why this scenario exists: when the API chat model (Gemini Flash Latest)
# is down the turn ends with only the "Operit" label and NO reply body (the
# old harness read that blank body as a PASS). EXPECT_REPLY records that in
# the run notes — the operator sees "model unavailable" in the report
# instead of a green run, but the walk does NOT abort (user directive
# 18.10: report it, don't crash). NOTE_IF_PRESENT also reports the
# ErrorDialog form (title R.string.request_failed = "Request Failed") if it
# does pop.

EXPECT 15 Enter your question...
MAYBE_TAP New Chat
EXPECT Enter your question...
REPLY_BASE
TAP Enter your question...
TYPE ping
TAP Send
# The model call spends a while in flight; wait for a real reply body. A
# missing body is recorded as a note (model unavailable), not a failure.
EXPECT_REPLY 120
# The dialog form of the failure is reported too, never crashes the run.
NOTE_IF_PRESENT Request Failed
DUMP
